\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
\label{nonsisa}
\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
Given two positive integers $a,b$ such that $a\cdot b \leq g$ we have the canonical inclusions
\begin{equation} \label{eq:nonsisa}
\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
\mathfrak{h}^{a\cdot b}(A)=\textnormal{Sym}^{a \cdot b} \mathfrak{h}^1(A) \subset (\textnormal{Sym}^{a} \mathfrak{h}^1(A))^{\otimes b}  = \mathfrak{h}^a(A)^{\otimes b}.
\end{equation}
  induced by Theorem \ref{classic}(\ref{kunn}). In particular any pairing on the right hand side induces a pairing on the left hand side.

\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
\label{accoppiamenti1}
\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
Fix an integer $n$ such that   $ 2 \leq 2n\leq g.$ Then the three motivic pairings $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{1,\mathrm{mot}}^{\otimes 2n}$,  $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{2,\mathrm{mot}}^{\otimes n}$ and $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{2n,\mathrm{mot}}$ on $\mathfrak{h}^{2n,\mathrm{prim}}(A)\in \mathrm{NUM}(k)_{\mathbb Q}$ coincide up to a positive rational scalar. Moreover, for each of these pairings, the Lefschetz decomposition $\mathfrak{h}^{2n}(A) = \mathfrak{h}^{2n,\mathrm{prim}}(A) \oplus \mathfrak{h}^{2n-2,\mathrm{prim}}(A) (-1)$ is orthogonal.

\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
\label{oklefschetz}
\source{standard-conjectures-abelian-fourfolds}
Fix an integer $n$ such that   $ 2 \leq 2n\leq g.$ The pairings $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{1,\mathrm{mot} }^{\otimes 2n}$,  $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{2,\mathrm{mot}}^{\otimes n}$ and $\langle \cdot, \cdot \rangle_{2n,\mathrm{mot}} $  on  $\mathcal{Z}^{n}_{\mathrm{num}}(A)_{{\mathbb Q}}$ are positive definite if and only if anyone of them is so. Moreover, they are positive definite on $\mathcal{L}^{n}(A)$.

