\source{anticyclotomic-iwasawa-rational-elliptic-eisenstein}
\label{thm:E}
\source{anticyclotomic-iwasawa-rational-elliptic-eisenstein}
Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be an elliptic curve and $p>2$ an Eisenstein prime for $E$, so that $E[p]^{ss}=\mathbb{F}_p(\phi)\oplus\mathbb{F}_p(\psi)$ as $G_{\mathbb Q}$-modules, and assume that $\phi\vert_{G_p}\neq\mathds{1},\omega$. Let $r\in\{0,1\}$. Then the following implication holds:
\[






{\rm corank}_{{\mathbb Z}_p}{\rm Sel}_{p^\infty}(E/{\mathbb Q})=r
\;\Longrightarrow\;
{\rm ord}_{s=1}L(E,s)=r,
\]
and so ${\rm rank}_{\mathbb Z} E({\mathbb Q})=r$ and $\#\sha(E/{\mathbb Q})<\infty$.

\source{anticyclotomic-iwasawa-rational-elliptic-eisenstein}
\label{thm:F}
\source{anticyclotomic-iwasawa-rational-elliptic-eisenstein}
Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:E}, assume in addition that $\phi$ is either ramified at $p$ and odd, or unramified at $p$ and even. If ${\rm ord}_{s=1}L(E,s)=1$, then 
\[
{\rm ord}_{p}\biggl(\frac{L'(E, 1)}{\operatorname{Reg}(E / {\mathbb Q}) \cdot \Omega_{E}}\biggr)={\rm ord}_{p}\biggl(\# \sha(E / {\mathbb Q}) \prod_{\ell \nmid \infty} c_{\ell}(E /{\mathbb Q})\biggr),
\]
where 
\begin{itemize}
\item ${\rm Reg}(E/{\mathbb Q})$ is the regulator of $E({\mathbb Q})$, 
\item $\Omega_E=\int_{E(\mathbb{R})}\vert\omega_E\vert$ is the N\'{e}ron  period associated to the N\'{e}ron differential $\omega_E$, and
\item $c_\ell(E/{\mathbb Q})$ is the Tamagawa number of $E$ at the prime $\ell$.
\end{itemize} 
In other words, the $p$-part of the Birch--Swinnerton-Dyler formula for $E$ holds.

