\label{probertini}Let $Y$ be a projective variety over an algebraically closed field $k$.
\source{geometric-bogomolov-conjecture-arbitrary-characteristics}
Let $V$ be a closed subvariety of $Y$ of codimension $r\geq 1$ such that $Y$ is smooth at $\eta_V.$
Let $Z_1,\dots,Z_m$ be irreducible subvarieties of $Y$.
Assume that 
\begin{points}
\item[$\bullet$] $(\cup_{i=1}^m Z_i)\cap V$ is finite; 
\item[$\bullet$] $(\cup_{i=1}^m Z_i)\cap V\subseteq Y^{{\rm sm}}\cap V^{{\rm sm}}$.
\end{points}
Let $H$ be a Cartier divisor on $Y$ such that ${\mathcal O}_Y(H)\otimes I_V$ is generated by global sections, where
 $I_V\subset {\mathcal O}_Y$ is the ideal sheaf associated to $V$.
Every section $s\in H^0({\mathcal O}_Y(H)\otimes I_V)$ defines a divisor 
$H_s\in |H|$ via the inclusion $H^0({\mathcal O}_Y(H)\otimes I_V)\hookrightarrow H^0({\mathcal O}_Y(H)).$
Then for general elements 
$$(s_1,\dots, s_r)\in H^0({\mathcal O}_Y(H)\otimes I_V)^r,$$ 
the following holds:
\begin{points}
\item $H_{s_1}\cap\dots\cap H_{s_r}$ is a proper intersection in $Y$;
\item $H_{s_1}\cdots H_{s_r}=V+W$ where $W$ is an effective $(\dim Y-r)$-cycle such that 
$V\not\subseteq {\rm Supp} \,W$, and $W\cap Z_i$ is a proper intersection for every $i=1,\dots,m$.
\end{points}

