$$h^1(\Gamma_\delta) = h^1(\tilde \Gamma_\delta)\, .$$
Given $r$, the map $W_{\Gamma_\delta,r} \to W_{\tilde \Gamma_\delta, r}$ of admissible weightings mod $r$ (induced by the inclusion $H(\tilde \Gamma) \to H(\Gamma)$ of half-edge sets) is a bijection. 

Moreover, if the map $\Gamma_{\delta}\to\tilde{\Gamma}_{\delta}$ only contracts components with $$(\g(v),\n(v),\delta(v))=(0,2,0)\,,$$ there is a canonical isomorphism ${\rm Aut}(\Gamma_\delta) \cong {\rm Aut}(\tilde \Gamma_\delta)$. On the other hand, in the formula for ${\mathbb P}_g^\bullet$, every term such that $\Gamma_\delta$ has a vertex with $$(\g(v), \n(v), \delta(v))=(0,1,0)$$ necessarily vanishes. Indeed, the half-edge $h$ at this vertex must have $w(h)=0$ such that the corresponding edge term vanishes. 

