 \label{mine}
\source{refined-brill-noether-theory-hurwitz-spaces}
If $E$ is a vector bundle on $\pi: B \times \pp^1 \rightarrow B$ and ${\rm codim} \Sigmabar_{\vec{e}}(E) = u(\vec{e})$, then the class $[\Sigmabar_{\vec{e}}(E)]$ is given by a universal formula in terms of Chern classes $\pi_* E(m)$ and $\pi_*E(m-1)$ for suitably large $m$. Moreover, if this expected class is non-zero, then $\Sigmabar_{\vec{e}}(E)$ is non-empty.

\source{refined-brill-noether-theory-hurwitz-spaces}
 \label{cE}
\source{refined-brill-noether-theory-hurwitz-spaces}
Let $f\colon  C \rightarrow \pp^1$ be a curve of genus $g$ with a degree $k$ map to $\pp^1$. 
Let $\mathcal{L}$ be a Poincar\'e line bundle on $C \times {\rm Pic}^d(C)$ and let ${\mathbb E} = (f \times \mathrm{id})_* \mathcal{L}$ on $\pp^1 \times {\rm Pic}^d(C)$. Let $\pi: \pp^1 \times {\rm Pic}^d(C) \rightarrow {\rm Pic}^d(C)$ be the projection.
Let $\theta$ denote the class of the theta divisor on ${\rm Pic}^d(C) = \Jac(C)$.
Then we have $c_i(\pi_*{\mathbb E}(m)) = (-1)^i\theta^i/i!$ modulo classes supported on ${\rm Supp}(R^1\pi_*{\mathbb E}(m))$. The total Chern class is $c(\pi_*{\mathbb E}(m)) = e^{-\theta}$ away from ${\rm Supp}(R^1\pi_*{\mathbb E}(m))$.

We have a commutative diagram
\begin{center}
\begin{tikzcd}
& C \arrow{r}{f} & \pp^1 \\
&C \times {\rm Pic}^d(C) \arrow{u}{\alpha} \arrow{r}{f \times \mathrm{id}} \arrow{rd}[swap]{\nu} & \arrow{u}[swap]{\beta} \pp^1 \times {\rm Pic}^d(C) \arrow{d}{\pi}\\
& & {\rm Pic}^d(C)
\end{tikzcd}
\end{center}
Let $H = f^*(\O_{\pp^1}(1))$.
By the projection formula, 
\[{\mathbb E}(m) = ((f\times \mathrm{id})_* \L) \otimes \beta^* \O_{\pp^1}(m) =(f \times \mathrm{id})_*(\L \otimes \alpha^* H^{\otimes m}),\]
and so $\pi_*{\mathbb E}(m) = \nu_*(\L \otimes \alpha^* H^{\otimes m})$. We have that $\L \otimes \alpha^*H^{\otimes m}$ is the pullback of a Poincar\'e line bundle on $C \times {\rm Pic}^{d+mk}(C)$ via the identification ${\rm Pic}^d(C) \rightarrow {\rm Pic}^{d+mk}(C)$ given by tensoring with $H^{\otimes m}$. The calculation in \cite[p. 336]{ACGH} determines the Chern classes of the push forward of a Poincar\'e line bundle $\nu_*(\L \otimes \alpha^*H^{\otimes m})$ away from ${\rm Supp}(R^1\nu_*(\L \otimes \alpha^*H^{\otimes m})) = {\rm Supp}(R^1 \pi_*{\mathbb E}(m))$.

 \label{revisit}
\source{refined-brill-noether-theory-hurwitz-spaces}
Continuing Example \ref{Geoff}, the classes of the Brill-Noether splitting degeneracy loci on ${\rm Pic}^4(C)$ for $C$ a general trigonal curve of genus $5$ are
\[[\Sigmabar_{(-2, -1, 0)}({\mathbb E})] = \theta, \qquad [\Sigmabar_{(-2, -2, 1)}({\mathbb E})] = [\Sigmabar_{(-3, 0, 0)}({\mathbb E})] = \frac{\theta^4}{24}, \qquad [\Sigmabar_{(-3, -1, 1)}({\mathbb E})] = \frac{\theta^5}{60}.\]
The first three classes are computed using \cite[Lemma 5.1]{L}. The last class comes from twisting and substituting the Chern classes from Lemma \ref{cE} into the universal formula found in \cite[Example 6.2]{L}. Notice that $[\Sigmabar_{(-3, -1, 1)}({\mathbb E})]$ is twice the class of a point, as found in Example \ref{Geoff}.
Also, $[W^1_4(C)] = [\Sigmabar_{(-2, -2, 1)}({\mathbb E})] + [\Sigmabar_{(-3, 0, 0)}({\mathbb E})] = \frac{\theta^4}{12}$ is the class computed by Kempf-Kleimann-Laksov \cite{K, KL1, KL2}.

